WEBVTT

00:01:08.860 --> 00:01:10.980
SWORD GAI

00:01:37.720 --> 00:01:40.050
"Few people understand the wide gap

00:01:40.140 --> 00:01:43.680
between the image of a job
and the actual job itself."

00:01:44.470 --> 00:01:47.390
"Because of this,
an alarming number of new..."

00:01:58.410 --> 00:02:01.280
Hey, Sayaka, want to eat lunch outside?

00:02:01.620 --> 00:02:04.540
The weather's nice today,
so it'll feel great.

00:02:05.540 --> 00:02:06.750
Oh, sure.

00:02:08.170 --> 00:02:12.420
Sayaka, did you hear a new karaoke place
opened in front of the station?

00:02:12.750 --> 00:02:16.970
And get this, it's in 3D!
Let's check it out on our way home!

00:02:17.760 --> 00:02:20.470
I'm... kind of busy today.

00:02:20.550 --> 00:02:23.850
What, again? You're always busy.

00:02:23.930 --> 00:02:26.220
Really, you never want to hang out.

00:02:26.770 --> 00:02:28.140
Sorry.

00:02:28.850 --> 00:02:32.150
Hey, what's going on
with Ishii from the soccer team?

00:02:33.320 --> 00:02:34.610
Nothing, why?

00:02:34.690 --> 00:02:38.530
-What? He asked you out, right?
-Don't tell me you turned him down!

00:02:39.030 --> 00:02:43.700
I didn't, but...
I don't have time to spend with him.

00:02:43.780 --> 00:02:45.200
What do you mean?

00:02:45.290 --> 00:02:48.290
Do you have another guy you like
or something?

00:02:48.790 --> 00:02:50.330
No, that's not it.

00:02:53.290 --> 00:02:58.220
Then what's the problem?
Ishii's the captain of the soccer team!

00:02:58.300 --> 00:03:00.760
And he's cute and gets great grades!

00:03:01.300 --> 00:03:02.760
Y-Yeah.

00:03:02.930 --> 00:03:05.560
So, he's kind of too good for me.

00:03:05.640 --> 00:03:07.640
Jeez, what are you doing?

00:03:07.720 --> 00:03:11.600
I can't believe it!
I think I'm going crazy!

00:03:13.270 --> 00:03:15.190
This isn't funny!

00:03:15.270 --> 00:03:17.690
You're really weird, Sayaka.

00:03:18.400 --> 00:03:19.690
S-Sorry.

00:03:39.970 --> 00:03:41.510
Welcome home, miss.

00:03:43.590 --> 00:03:44.850
Tatsumi.

00:03:44.930 --> 00:03:47.310
The master asked me to run an errand.

00:03:47.760 --> 00:03:52.270
I see. That must be hard.
My father can be rough on people.

00:03:59.530 --> 00:04:00.360
Gai!

00:04:04.610 --> 00:04:06.160
Wait, Gai!

00:04:16.210 --> 00:04:20.800
You saved me back there, Gai.
I don't really know how to handle Tatsumi.

00:04:21.340 --> 00:04:22.720
I didn't save you.

00:04:23.800 --> 00:04:28.100
Hey, did you know that the karaoke place
in front of the station is in 3D?

00:04:28.220 --> 00:04:29.970
Let's go check it out!

00:04:30.850 --> 00:04:31.980
I've got work to do.

00:04:32.270 --> 00:04:36.860
Again? You've always got work,
and you never want to go anywhere.

00:04:37.650 --> 00:04:41.280
Even Father said you don't know
how to have fun.

00:04:41.740 --> 00:04:44.700
And if you're too serious,
you can't make a good sword.

00:04:46.990 --> 00:04:48.330
Did that upset you?

00:04:49.160 --> 00:04:50.660
I was joking!

00:04:51.540 --> 00:04:53.120
Enough. Get lost.

00:04:53.460 --> 00:04:54.460
What?

00:04:54.660 --> 00:04:56.330
-How rude.
-Give it back!

00:04:56.420 --> 00:04:58.840
Nope!
Not unless you come hang out with me!

00:04:59.340 --> 00:05:00.170
Ow!

00:05:00.630 --> 00:05:01.710
What are you doing?

00:05:01.800 --> 00:05:03.760
How dare you touch her!

00:05:03.840 --> 00:05:06.590
No, Tatsumi! It's my fault!

00:05:06.890 --> 00:05:08.720
I interrupted him during his work!

00:05:09.510 --> 00:05:12.640
No, it's Gai's fault
for letting you interfere.

00:05:13.100 --> 00:05:13.980
Well, Gai?

00:05:15.770 --> 00:05:17.190
You're right, Tatsumi.

00:05:17.900 --> 00:05:18.810
I'm sorry.

00:05:19.230 --> 00:05:22.940
Are those the eyes of someone
who's apologizing?

00:05:23.490 --> 00:05:24.610
Is there a problem?

00:05:26.700 --> 00:05:27.950
What's going on here?

00:05:29.950 --> 00:05:30.780
Father!

00:05:30.870 --> 00:05:32.700
Master, Gai was--

00:05:32.990 --> 00:05:36.210
I-It's nothing.
We were just playing around.

00:05:40.040 --> 00:05:44.590
The Shiryu has begun to cry once more.
Tomorrow we perform the calming ritual.

00:05:44.670 --> 00:05:47.590
Sayaka, purify yourself
for the role of priestess.

00:05:47.930 --> 00:05:48.840
Y-Yes sir.

00:05:49.760 --> 00:05:51.470
Gai, come with me.

00:05:52.060 --> 00:05:52.930
Yes sir.

00:06:03.690 --> 00:06:05.190
Why do you not pray?

00:06:05.570 --> 00:06:10.740
This is your mother's grave,
and the place where you were born.

00:06:16.000 --> 00:06:22.380
I buried your mother here because
it has a clear view of the estate.

00:06:22.460 --> 00:06:25.210
So she could always watch over you.

00:06:27.260 --> 00:06:29.720
It's been over a decade
since I adopted you.

00:06:30.010 --> 00:06:31.970
You've finished your required education,

00:06:32.050 --> 00:06:36.060
and I want to hear
about your future plans.

00:06:37.930 --> 00:06:42.860
Let me stay with you forever.
I have no future except as a swordsmith.

00:06:44.860 --> 00:06:46.900
I thought you'd say that.

00:06:47.400 --> 00:06:49.990
Work even harder.
Your mother will be pleased.

00:06:51.620 --> 00:06:53.740
My mother will not be pleased.

00:06:54.950 --> 00:06:56.240
What do you mean?

00:06:59.000 --> 00:06:59.960
Nothing.

00:07:35.870 --> 00:07:36.700
<i>Gai?</i>

00:07:41.540 --> 00:07:45.040
<i>Shiryu, you are my only mother.</i>

00:07:46.710 --> 00:07:49.970
Now, moving on to item number 23.

00:07:50.420 --> 00:07:52.720
The "Sukhothai Buddha Statue."

00:07:53.550 --> 00:07:55.640
Bidding opens at 40,000 dollars.

00:07:56.680 --> 00:07:58.850
-50,000 dollars!
-60,000!

00:08:01.180 --> 00:08:02.100
This is good!

00:08:02.560 --> 00:08:04.400
<i>Enough playing around, Miki.</i>

00:08:04.900 --> 00:08:06.770
<i>You're not there to eat.</i>

00:08:07.520 --> 00:08:11.900
Don't be so prim and proper.
I haven't had a meal like this in a while.

00:08:11.990 --> 00:08:13.570
Oh, I'll take this wine too.

00:08:16.240 --> 00:08:18.490
It's great! I've never had this before.

00:08:18.580 --> 00:08:19.950
It's wonderful.

00:08:20.790 --> 00:08:23.000
This fragrance, it's a Richebourg.

00:08:24.210 --> 00:08:27.130
It's said to smell
like a bouquet of flowers.

00:08:27.880 --> 00:08:31.170
Though personally,
I prefer Romanée-Saint-Vivant.

00:08:44.230 --> 00:08:46.520
You're not participating in the auction?

00:08:47.730 --> 00:08:50.780
I think it's quite the item, that statue.

00:08:51.230 --> 00:08:55.990
Yes, I'm here for something else.
I’m just seeing how things are today.

00:08:56.070 --> 00:08:58.120
-100,000 dollars!
-102,000!

00:08:58.450 --> 00:09:00.540
The same as me.

00:09:00.990 --> 00:09:04.160
Then may we both win our bids.

00:09:04.250 --> 00:09:05.080
Cheers.

00:09:05.710 --> 00:09:07.040
Very well, sir.

00:09:07.500 --> 00:09:10.800
The "Sukhothai Buddha Statue"
goes to you for 130,000 dollars.

00:09:12.010 --> 00:09:13.510
What? Me?

00:09:15.510 --> 00:09:18.300
Congratulations. An excellent purchase.

00:09:20.720 --> 00:09:22.220
<i>What are you doing?</i>

00:09:22.680 --> 00:09:25.140
This is coming out of your pocket money.

00:09:25.770 --> 00:09:27.100
<i>N-No!</i>

00:09:30.360 --> 00:09:32.230
That concludes today's auction.

00:09:33.030 --> 00:09:35.860
The items for the next auction
are in another room.

00:09:36.070 --> 00:09:39.410
Please take a look at them
at your convenience.

00:10:06.060 --> 00:10:07.230
<i>Well, is it real?</i>

00:10:16.780 --> 00:10:19.910
It's making me sick. It's laughing.

00:10:19.990 --> 00:10:21.490
The Azoth Sword, yes?

00:10:22.620 --> 00:10:24.580
Is this what you're after?

00:10:24.660 --> 00:10:25.620
You too, then?

00:10:26.080 --> 00:10:30.040
Yes. If it's real,
I'd certainly like to get my hands on it.

00:10:30.290 --> 00:10:35.670
After all, this sword was owned
by the legendary alchemist Paracelsus.

00:10:36.300 --> 00:10:40.090
You believe the story
of Paracelsus and the devil?

00:10:40.760 --> 00:10:44.260
I don't know. But it is interesting.

00:10:45.100 --> 00:10:46.850
In the 16th century...

00:10:48.350 --> 00:10:51.650
Paracelsus made a contract with a devil,

00:10:52.110 --> 00:10:54.110
to master the arts of alchemy.

00:10:54.820 --> 00:10:59.650
In exchange,
he was to sell his soul to the devil.

00:11:00.780 --> 00:11:02.490
With the devil's knowledge,

00:11:02.700 --> 00:11:06.910
he was eventually able
to complete the Philosopher's Stone,

00:11:07.000 --> 00:11:08.450
the root of all creation.

00:11:08.960 --> 00:11:09.790
But...

00:11:11.290 --> 00:11:13.290
he broke the contract.

00:11:14.880 --> 00:11:19.970
That would make a devil mad.
He broke his promise to sell his soul.

00:11:20.220 --> 00:11:23.430
It makes sense
that he'd try to kill Paracelsus.

00:11:24.760 --> 00:11:27.850
But it was Paracelsus who was victorious.

00:11:29.310 --> 00:11:32.270
He sealed the devil
in the Philosopher's Stone,

00:11:32.350 --> 00:11:34.190
which he had placed on a sword.

00:11:44.410 --> 00:11:46.830
And that was the Azoth Sword.

00:11:53.460 --> 00:11:55.420
Well, Mr. Marcus?

00:11:56.750 --> 00:11:59.170
This time, it was real.

00:12:00.300 --> 00:12:01.970
I heard the devil's laughter.

00:12:19.860 --> 00:12:21.610
Gai was with the Shiryu?

00:12:22.110 --> 00:12:25.320
Yes. He kept staring at it
throughout the night.

00:12:26.530 --> 00:12:27.530
I know.

00:12:27.830 --> 00:12:31.200
You're not supposed to touch,
or even look at the Shiryu!

00:12:31.830 --> 00:12:35.420
That's because it's a danger
to those who do.

00:12:35.750 --> 00:12:37.960
But if it doesn't do harm,
it's no concern.

00:12:38.340 --> 00:12:41.130
Does that mean Gai is special?

00:12:42.380 --> 00:12:47.890
When I found Gai as a newborn,
next to his mother's corpse,

00:12:48.640 --> 00:12:51.430
his hands were holding the Shiryu tightly,

00:12:52.140 --> 00:12:55.560
as if it was keeping him alive.

00:12:56.600 --> 00:12:59.900
I believe the Shiryu seeks him, too.

00:13:00.440 --> 00:13:05.860
That's why we need Gai's blood to calm it.

00:13:08.160 --> 00:13:10.120
You've realized too, right?

00:13:10.790 --> 00:13:11.620
Gai's eyes...

00:13:12.660 --> 00:13:17.130
they don't see people,
but are always looking at the sword.

00:13:17.210 --> 00:13:19.000
You know what that means, right?

00:13:19.540 --> 00:13:22.090
He lives with death.

00:13:22.420 --> 00:13:26.590
A life where he'll be sliced apart
if he averts his eyes for an instant.

00:13:27.180 --> 00:13:29.300
Could you do that?

00:13:29.390 --> 00:13:30.970
I-I...

00:13:31.390 --> 00:13:33.430
Even I could not.

00:13:33.560 --> 00:13:38.730
Gai may have reached a state
that I long for but cannot achieve.

00:13:45.110 --> 00:13:48.740
We will now begin the calming ritual
for the Shiryu.

00:14:02.800 --> 00:14:04.130
Sayaka, enter.

00:14:04.670 --> 00:14:08.590
In heavenly fields the divine shall sit,
bearing the life of Kanayago,

00:14:09.640 --> 00:14:12.850
I call then, to all the gods,
that they may gather here.

00:14:16.680 --> 00:14:17.520
Gai.

00:14:32.450 --> 00:14:36.250
<i>I can't let this happen.
<i>Gai can't be the chosen one!</i></i>

00:14:48.840 --> 00:14:49.680
No!

00:15:34.970 --> 00:15:36.640
What's going on, Father?

00:15:37.010 --> 00:15:40.560
Gai's been out of the hospital a week,
but the pain hasn't let up!

00:15:41.310 --> 00:15:47.190
Gai is feeling the pain of his lost arm.
A pain that isn't real can't be cured.

00:15:47.570 --> 00:15:50.070
I don't understand. How did this happen?

00:15:50.650 --> 00:15:52.530
What happened during the Calming Ritual?

00:15:53.570 --> 00:15:54.990
Just an accident.

00:15:55.160 --> 00:15:57.160
It's none of your concern.

00:16:03.040 --> 00:16:03.960
Gai.

00:16:06.170 --> 00:16:07.040
G-Gai?

00:16:09.380 --> 00:16:10.550
Hang in there, Gai.

00:16:11.720 --> 00:16:13.930
I'm here for you.

00:16:18.510 --> 00:16:19.350
Gai!

00:16:22.890 --> 00:16:23.940
I'll kill you!

00:16:25.270 --> 00:16:26.310
I'll kill you!

00:16:28.520 --> 00:16:29.360
Gai!

00:16:29.440 --> 00:16:31.610
How can he defile a grave like that?

00:16:32.990 --> 00:16:35.280
This is the woman who abandoned me!

00:16:47.630 --> 00:16:48.540
Shiryu...

00:16:49.130 --> 00:16:53.800
Gai held you when he was a baby,
and you are his protector.

00:16:53.880 --> 00:16:56.260
So, become his arm and protect him!

00:16:56.720 --> 00:17:01.640
Or perhaps,
was this what you wanted, Shiryu?

00:17:12.530 --> 00:17:17.740
Now, on to item number 13,
the Azoth Sword.

00:17:18.320 --> 00:17:21.240
It's said the 15th century alchemist,
Paracelsus,

00:17:21.330 --> 00:17:23.830
sealed a devil in this legendary sword.

00:17:24.160 --> 00:17:26.250
Opening bid starts at 20,000 dollars.

00:17:26.580 --> 00:17:28.540
-30,000 dollars!
-50,000 dollars!

00:17:29.000 --> 00:17:29.960
60,000!

00:17:30.340 --> 00:17:31.300
80,000!

00:17:32.210 --> 00:17:33.550
500,000 dollars.

00:17:36.630 --> 00:17:40.430
F-Five hundred thousand?
What do we do, Kyoka?

00:17:40.510 --> 00:17:44.060
<i>Don't get scared.
<i>Our budget is infinite. Go.</i></i>

00:17:44.520 --> 00:17:47.100
If there's no other bids, then 500,000--

00:17:47.190 --> 00:17:48.150
Wait.

00:17:48.850 --> 00:17:49.900
1,000,000 dollars.

00:17:49.980 --> 00:17:51.940
<i>Don't raise it that fast, dummy!</i>

00:17:52.020 --> 00:17:53.940
1,200,000!

00:17:54.570 --> 00:17:56.070
1,300,000!

00:17:56.320 --> 00:17:59.120
-1,350,000!
-1,500,000 dollars!

00:18:01.200 --> 00:18:04.790
The current bid is 1,500,000 dollars.
Anyone else?

00:18:08.830 --> 00:18:12.040
Then the winning bid is 1,500,000 dollars.

00:18:18.550 --> 00:18:22.510
I did it, Kyoka.
I'll return to the Shoshidai immediately.

00:18:51.830 --> 00:18:54.670
I guess I don't need to ask what you want.

00:18:55.050 --> 00:18:59.050
I can tell from what's going on here.
You want the Azoth Sword, right?

00:18:59.470 --> 00:19:01.800
Who are you?

00:19:01.890 --> 00:19:05.060
Paying 1,500,000 dollars
for that old sword.

00:19:05.390 --> 00:19:07.850
I could ask the same question of you.

00:19:07.930 --> 00:19:12.020
But you don't understand
how dangerous the Azoth Sword is.

00:19:12.440 --> 00:19:14.270
It's not for an amateur to have.

00:19:14.940 --> 00:19:15.940
I know.

00:19:16.570 --> 00:19:19.320
That's why I need it.

00:19:19.860 --> 00:19:22.280
Sell it to me for a fair price.

00:19:22.620 --> 00:19:23.910
If you don't want to...

00:19:26.790 --> 00:19:30.670
Oh man, I saw that coming.
That's not going to work.

00:19:31.080 --> 00:19:33.380
No matter how strong you are,
a normal person...

00:19:49.310 --> 00:19:50.270
Impossible!

00:19:50.730 --> 00:19:52.650
See? Told you.

00:19:53.770 --> 00:19:55.360
I'll be going now.

00:20:02.410 --> 00:20:05.200
This time it's not a normal person.

00:20:06.120 --> 00:20:07.200
No!

00:20:08.660 --> 00:20:10.200
Administrator Miura?

00:20:10.620 --> 00:20:13.170
I see. I heard the rumors.

00:20:13.790 --> 00:20:16.460
You're Takuma Miura,
formerly of the Shoshidai.

00:20:16.540 --> 00:20:19.460
That is this one's old name.

00:20:19.550 --> 00:20:23.010
You called me, and I answered.

00:20:24.260 --> 00:20:25.220
My name is...

00:20:29.140 --> 00:20:30.350
Zsoltgewinn!

00:20:30.430 --> 00:20:34.100
<i>Miki, get out of there!
<i>You can't beat Zsoltgewinn alone!</i></i>

00:20:34.730 --> 00:20:36.770
I won't lose in a shouting match!

00:20:37.440 --> 00:20:39.230
Thunder, roar!

00:20:40.030 --> 00:20:41.440
Fallgon!

00:20:56.380 --> 00:20:57.330
This is...
